{"file":"Kubernetes Mastery-0.1.0-v2.zip","bytes":104032,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"kubernetes-mastery","displayName":"Kubernetes Mastery","description":"Reason about, author, and safely operate Kubernetes. Three skills: concepts (the founder/company mental model), authoring (failure-mode-first manifest design and review), and operating (read-only-by-default live-cluster triage). Grounded in official Kubernetes docs, the NSA/CISA Hardening Guide, OWASP Kubernetes Top 10, Pod Security Standards, and the CIS Benchmark.","version":"0.1.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/RegardV/kubernetes-mastery","homepage":"https://github.com/RegardV/kubernetes-mastery","keywords":["kubernetes","k8s","devops","sre","helm","rbac","security","eks","gke","troubleshooting"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/k8s-authoring/SKILL.md","name":"k8s-authoring","description":"Write, review, refactor, or migrate Kubernetes manifests, Helm charts, Kustomize overlays, or RBAC — anything that produces YAML you will apply to a cluster. Runs a failure-mode-first workflow (insecure defaults, resource starvation, network exposure, privilege sprawl, fragile rollouts, API drift), hardens against official standards (NSA/CISA, OWASP K8s Top 10, Pod Security Standards, CIS), and validates output before delivering. Use for \"create a Deployment\", \"review my manifest for production\", \"add RBAC/NetworkPolicy\", \"write a Helm chart\".","headings":["Kubernetes Authoring — failure-mode-first","Workflow (follow in order)","The six failure modes","Grounding"],"name_hint":"k8s · authoring"},{"path":"skills/k8s-concepts/SKILL.md","name":"k8s-concepts","description":"Explain, teach, or reason about how Kubernetes fits together — the control plane, nodes, workloads, networking, and the reconciliation loop — using a founder-running-a-company mental model. Use before making an architecture decision, when someone asks \"how does X work\" or \"why does Kubernetes do Y\", or when another Kubernetes task needs conceptual grounding. Grounds the k8s-authoring and k8s-operating skills.","headings":["Kubernetes Concepts — think like a founder running a company","The one-line model","The layers (teach in this order)","How to use the references","Hand-off"],"name_hint":"k8s · concepts"},{"path":"skills/k8s-operating/SKILL.md","name":"k8s-operating","description":"Troubleshoot or audit a live Kubernetes cluster with kubectl — investigate crashes (CrashLoopBackOff, OOMKilled, Pending, ImagePullBackOff), read events and logs, trace ownership chains, and check RBAC/security/network posture. Read-only by default; proposes but never runs mutating or destructive commands without explicit user confirmation. Use for \"why is my pod crashing\", \"what's wrong with this deployment\", \"audit my cluster\", \"debug this service\".","headings":["Kubernetes Operating — safe live-cluster triage","Safety contract (non-negotiable)","Triage workflow","References","Homelab note"],"name_hint":"k8s · operating"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Kubernetes Mastery","Skills","Shared cloud references","Example prompts","Install","Validate","Design","Credits & prior art","License"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json","CHANGELOG.md","LICENSE","README.md","docs/CARD.md","docs/DESIGN.md","docs/STORY.md","references/conditional/aks.md","references/conditional/eks.md","references/conditional/gke.md","references/conditional/openshift.md","scripts/validate.sh","skills/k8s-authoring/SKILL.md","skills/k8s-authoring/references/examples-good-bad.md","skills/k8s-authoring/references/failure-modes.md","skills/k8s-authoring/references/networking-storage.md","skills/k8s-authoring/references/packaging-validation.md","skills/k8s-authoring/references/security-hardening.md","skills/k8s-authoring/references/workload-patterns.md","skills/k8s-concepts/SKILL.md","skills/k8s-concepts/r